Mechanisms:
- Session retains Config/readiness, watches, child control pipes and a stored recovery task. Cancellation cannot lose a partial child handshake. Wire readers stay bounded (8 replies). Known loss returns promptly to IO's bounded retained queue. Failed startup produces a held disconnected state rather than repeatedly advancing process generations. Shutdown aborts pending startup and reaps installed children.
- Logic-only restart preserves supervisor/PTYS and process generations; refreshed catalogue and authoritative watch snapshots are delivered on the existing Event::Reply seam.
- Supervisor recovery implementation saves explicit cwd/role/overlay inputs (never inherited environment), replays committed prior ring into Playback, changes process generation, resets the new capture cursor and records an explicit loss gap. It rebuilds overlays/capabilities and uses existing launch planner resume flags. Old rings remain separate for later history work.
- Natural process exit marks launch state non-running, so general recovery does not deliberately resurrect it. Close/history retained-view behavior belongs C1c-2, not claimed here.

